course: dictionary
lesson: 15025
title: Saying it again
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To restate something is to say it again, often in different and clearer words. The prefix re- means again, so restate means state again. «The teacher asked us to restate the question in our own words.» She wanted the same idea said again so that it was easier to understand.
explain: Writers do this too. «Her last paragraph restated the main idea of the whole essay.» The idea comes back at the end, so the reader remembers it. Restating is not the same as copying: the words are changed to make the meaning clearer.
explain: In its formal sense, restate means to say a rule, view or promise again, firmly. «The judge restated the rule: no phones in court.» The word shows that the rule was said again so that nobody could forget it.
fact: Restate means to say something again.
fact: Restating often uses different, clearer words.
fact: «Restate the question» means say the question again in your own words before you answer.
fact: «Restate the main idea» is a common tip for finishing a piece of writing.
fact: In a formal sense, «restate a promise» means to say the promise again, firmly.
exercise: «Please restate the rule so everyone can hear it.» What does restate mean here? | Forget it completely | Sing it loudly | Throw it away | *Say it again, clearly
exercise: Which is the best way to restate «The cat sat on the mat»? | The cat jumped over the fence | The cat sat on the bed | *The mat was where the cat was sitting | The mat sat on the cat
exercise: Which word is closest in meaning to restate? | Dance | Hide | *Repeat | Forget
test: «The head teacher restated the school promise.» In this sentence, what does restate mean? | *Said the promise again, firmly | Forgot the promise | Broke the promise | Wrote a brand new school
test: Why might you restate a question before answering it? | *To check that you understand it | To hide the answer | To fill up the page
exam: Which sentence uses restate correctly? | The river restated its colour | Ben restated the big spider in the bath | Mia restated her shoes in the cupboard | *Ali restated his plan for the project in clearer words
